(3721824, 507690, 6804, '<td valign="top">A very emotive capture!  Not many stop to think about the death of a hummingbird.  They are beautiful and fragile creatures that are universally loved.  This shot shows the beauty gone.  The darkness in the shot replaces everything that was once bright and full of life and color.  The drops on the glass are as tears.  Even the vertical strut is crooked giving the feeling that something is terribly wrong. <br/>High marks from me on this one.  I hope this one doesnt just get tossed into the middle of the pile because it isnt the typical portrait of a hummingbird.  Good luck with this one.</td>', 'A very emotive capture!  Not many stop to think about the death of a hummingbird.  They are beautiful and fragile creatures that are universally loved.  This shot shows the beauty gone.  The darkness in the shot replaces everything that was once bright and full of life and color.  The drops on the glass are as tears.  Even the vertical strut is crooked giving the feeling that something is terribly wrong. High marks from me on this one.  I hope this one doesnt just get tossed into the middle of the pile because it isnt the typical portrait of a hummingbird.  Good luck with this one.', '2007-06-01 01:30:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(3721839, 524424, 41337, '<td valign="top">I like the POV but I feel the impact could be better if you had him in a different part of the frame. Having him higher up is probably more cliche but it would heighten the airborne feeling, IMO. Heck just a 90 degree rotate might give this a totally different feel. Anyway just my thoughts.</td>', 'I like the POV but I feel the impact could be better if you had him in a different part of the frame. Having him higher up is probably more cliche but it would heighten the airborne feeling, IMO. Heck just a 90 degree rotate might give this a totally different feel. Anyway just my thoughts.', '2007-06-01 01:33:36.000000', NULL, 1),
