(3756304, 520829, 69325, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by alonzo4b:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks for the comments.   Clearly from the comments it appears that what I thought was interesting did not go over too well.  The woman in the front is too hot and that was unintended.  I did, however, intentionally put the woman in the back in the heavy shadow.  I just thought that would be an interesting contrast between the two.  I have a tendency to enter pics that are somewhat unconventional and perhaps my instincts are a bit off. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>i would encourage you to follow your instincts....the critiques offered on this sight defiantly have value but in my estimation there are no hard and fast rules in photography, you should ALWAYS shoot what you enjoy...</td>', 'Originally posted by alonzo4b: Thanks for the comments.   Clearly from the comments it appears that what I thought was interesting did not go over too well.  The woman in the front is too hot and that was unintended.  I did, however, intentionally put the woman in the back in the heavy shadow.  I just thought that would be an interesting contrast between the two.  I have a tendency to enter pics that are somewhat unconventional and perhaps my instincts are a bit off.   i would encourage you to follow your instincts....the critiques offered on this sight defiantly have value but in my estimation there are no hard and fast rules in photography, you should ALWAYS shoot what you enjoy...', '2007-06-08 07:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
