(3756368, 524949, 74979, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lowcivicman99:</b></div><hr/><i> It looks like you were outside and you used your flash. Also I think that the edges of the flower look like they have a halo around them as if you blurred the background and outlined the flower with the marquee and feathered it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi~  I didn''t use the flash, and as for the effects around the petal edges, this was a puzzler to me...  I assume the things you mention above (marquee, feathered) are PS tools?  I have yet to start using the PhotoShop!  Looking at what limited processing I did do, can anyone give me a clue as to why the "halo" effect occurred?   just curious..I actually like this photgraph a lot, but as I say, was puzzled by this effect...<br/> <br/>Thanks a lot for the nice comments!<br/>Anni</td>', 'Originally posted by Lowcivicman99: It looks like you were outside and you used your flash. Also I think that the edges of the flower look like they have a halo around them as if you blurred the background and outlined the flower with the marquee and feathered it.   Hi~  I didn''t use the flash, and as for the effects around the petal edges, this was a puzzler to me...  I assume the things you mention above (marquee, feathered) are PS tools?  I have yet to start using the PhotoShop!  Looking at what limited processing I did do, can anyone give me a clue as to why the "halo" effect occurred?   just curious..I actually like this photgraph a lot, but as I say, was puzzled by this effect... Thanks a lot for the nice comments!Anni', '2007-06-08 08:00:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3756376, 524073, 19708, '<td valign="top">Yeah, suppose any of them would do.<br/>Wish the site had a mechanism in place that required a why on vote extremes, high or low. I saw no comments during the challenge that would suggest a low vote such as that.  Like I said, the score was not the issue, as I really don''t care if it ended up with 162 votes of 6 and a single 1, so long as the person could at least tell me why they voted a 1.<br/> <br/>I know - lemme go find the beating a dead horse icon....<br/> <br/>Oh - you forgot one:<br/>"I''m sorry, I just got over a bad case of Jaundice and now I hate Yellow"<br/> <br/>hehehehehehe</td>', 'Yeah, suppose any of them would do.Wish the site had a mechanism in place that required a why on vote extremes, high or low. I saw no comments during the challenge that would suggest a low vote such as that.  Like I said, the score was not the issue, as I really don''t care if it ended up with 162 votes of 6 and a single 1, so long as the person could at least tell me why they voted a 1. I know - lemme go find the beating a dead horse icon.... Oh - you forgot one:"I''m sorry, I just got over a bad case of Jaundice and now I hate Yellow" hehehehehehe', '2007-06-08 08:01:52.000000', NULL, 0),
