(3756719, 524949, 50641, '<td valign="top">Was the halo effect in the original?  Sometimes this effect can be achieved by a combination of overexposure plus off-focus (both particular to the purple flower only, in this case). To support this, there doesn''t seem to be a halo on the parts of the purple plant that are in focus.  But, if you didn''t see it until after you processed the photo, it possibly could be due to sharpening before you saturated. In any case, I think it''s a pretty cool effect!</td>', 'Was the halo effect in the original?  Sometimes this effect can be achieved by a combination of overexposure plus off-focus (both particular to the purple flower only, in this case). To support this, there doesn''t seem to be a halo on the parts of the purple plant that are in focus.  But, if you didn''t see it until after you processed the photo, it possibly could be due to sharpening before you saturated. In any case, I think it''s a pretty cool effect!', '2007-06-08 10:15:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(3756725, 524618, 70514, '<td valign="top">Well, it just goes to show you that they either like it or don''t, huh?  I love this kind of processing, but you know that.  Oh well.  It''s a great image, nice composition, and I love the angle.</td>', 'Well, it just goes to show you that they either like it or don''t, huh?  I love this kind of processing, but you know that.  Oh well.  It''s a great image, nice composition, and I love the angle.', '2007-06-08 10:16:56.000000', NULL, 0),
