(3763450, 507983, 55838, '<td valign="top">It''s really a shame you got rid of the "monkey poo yellow/brown" - it''s my favorite.  Isn''t that a crayola crayon color?  : )  Very nice shot and a terrific score.  Congratulations!  Brilliant greens and an interesting little model.  Well done.  I didn''t vote in this challenge.</td>', 'It''s really a shame you got rid of the "monkey poo yellow/brown" - it''s my favorite.  Isn''t that a crayola crayon color?  : )  Very nice shot and a terrific score.  Congratulations!  Brilliant greens and an interesting little model.  Well done.  I didn''t vote in this challenge.', '2007-06-10 15:41:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3763529, 524592, 55838, '<td valign="top">Awwwww how cute!  I like the color tones - especially on the back and the bokeh is very nice. DOF is very cool too.  My eyes would prefer at least part of the squirrel to be in sharper focus.  Great border and nicely composed. I didn''t vote on this image.</td>', 'Awwwww how cute!  I like the color tones - especially on the back and the bokeh is very nice. DOF is very cool too.  My eyes would prefer at least part of the squirrel to be in sharper focus.  Great border and nicely composed. I didn''t vote on this image.', '2007-06-10 16:12:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3763912, 524468, 68035, '<td valign="top">Peter<br/> <br/>I''m in a bit of a quandry, not sure whether I am more jealous of the fact that you have such a wonderful visitor or the fact that even if it came to my place I dont know whether I would be able to capture it half as well as you<br/> <br/>Great job and wonderful dof</td>', 'Peter I''m in a bit of a quandry, not sure whether I am more jealous of the fact that you have such a wonderful visitor or the fact that even if it came to my place I dont know whether I would be able to capture it half as well as you Great job and wonderful dof', '2007-06-10 18:29:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3763958, 520995, 68035, '<td valign="top">I really like this pic Roz, dont know why but it has a real old day feel to it as if the lad taking it may have been playing in a bomb crater<br/> <br/>Stunning focus and I love the fact that the boy is oof without losing one iota of the wonderful iimpish expression he has<br/> <br/></td>', 'I really like this pic Roz, dont know why but it has a real old day feel to it as if the lad taking it may have been playing in a bomb crater Stunning focus and I love the fact that the boy is oof without losing one iota of the wonderful iimpish expression he has ', '2007-06-10 18:41:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3763978, 520404, 68035, '<td valign="top">Cant believe that this one did not score and finish higher even in a free study challenge<br/> <br/>The main splash is wonderful and the focus works wonderfully with the bokeh.  the railing is a great addition as well as it draws you into and then through the wave splash<br/> <br/>B&amp;W was also the perfect choice as it means you have no distractions to the moment of impact that you have captured so well<br/> <br/></td>', 'Cant believe that this one did not score and finish higher even in a free study challenge The main splash is wonderful and the focus works wonderfully with the bokeh.  the railing is a great addition as well as it draws you into and then through the wave splash B&W was also the perfect choice as it means you have no distractions to the moment of impact that you have captured so well ', '2007-06-10 18:47:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3764040, 522481, 68035, '<td valign="top">Gee Jack you really took a bit of a mauling on this one.  However what I would say is that if you look at the 8s 9s and 10''s (FOUR!!!!) that you got it echos what I said during my in competition post.  Whilst it did not do it for me there are people who have loved this image to score it very well which shows the experiment worked because it is better (IMO) to have got a range of scores which include the very highest ones than simply 4s 5s and 6s<br/> <br/></td>', 'Gee Jack you really took a bit of a mauling on this one.  However what I would say is that if you look at the 8s 9s and 10''s (FOUR!!!!) that you got it echos what I said during my in competition post.  Whilst it did not do it for me there are people who have loved this image to score it very well which shows the experiment worked because it is better (IMO) to have got a range of scores which include the very highest ones than simply 4s 5s and 6s ', '2007-06-10 19:05:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(3764049, 510550, 68035, '<td valign="top">Joe<br/> <br/>Well I have to be honest and sat when I flew over the hoover dam and took my picture I was at least thinking it would be the best dam shot in the free study and then you went and trumped me with this one<br/> <br/>Wonderful image....<br/> <br/>I think we could call it an honourable draw in terms of best pun used in the title though</td>', 'Joe Well I have to be honest and sat when I flew over the hoover dam and took my picture I was at least thinking it would be the best dam shot in the free study and then you went and trumped me with this one Wonderful image.... I think we could call it an honourable draw in terms of best pun used in the title though', '2007-06-10 19:07:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3764068, 520995, 60915, '<td valign="top">whoa! I see a girl standing in this shot as well...</td>', 'whoa! I see a girl standing in this shot as well...', '2007-06-10 19:13:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(3764243, 524520, 66597, '<td valign="top">Wow, Fernando, didn''t realize this was yours when voting! What a beautiful photograph and great showing. The depth is just spectacular here.</td>', 'Wow, Fernando, didn''t realize this was yours when voting! What a beautiful photograph and great showing. The depth is just spectacular here.', '2007-06-10 20:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3764360, 524272, 55838, '<td valign="top">Such a fantastically emotive shot.  This split second in time seems to speak volumes about these two people and their love for one another. Such a tenderness, quiet shared joy, a speck of majesty, and wee bit of sadness all wrapped up in one moment.  Love the deep dark tones and the contrast.  Exquisite photograph.  I''ll go ahead and join the masses and make this a favorite - if I could do it twice, I would.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-10 20:00:50.</i></td>', 'Such a fantastically emotive shot.  This split second in time seems to speak volumes about these two people and their love for one another. Such a tenderness, quiet shared joy, a speck of majesty, and wee bit of sadness all wrapped up in one moment.  Love the deep dark tones and the contrast.  Exquisite photograph.  I''ll go ahead and join the masses and make this a favorite - if I could do it twice, I would.', '2007-06-10 21:00:00.000000', '2007-06-10 21:00:50.000000', 0),
(3764521, 525036, 42013, '<td valign="top">You never leave the viewer disapointed. Congrats on top 10!</td>', 'You never leave the viewer disapointed. Congrats on top 10!', '2007-06-10 21:48:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3765234, 524146, 77250, '<td valign="top">I think this shot deserved a higher rating than it got.  It really should not have been in the last 100.  The one thing that I would say is that the sky is a little blown out.  Some clouds would help break it up so its not so white or a tad less on the exposure side would have helped a bit.  I''ll email you what I did to change the photo.  All I did was crop it a bit and change the saturation.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-06-10 23:11:42.</i></td>', 'I think this shot deserved a higher rating than it got.  It really should not have been in the last 100.  The one thing that I would say is that the sky is a little blown out.  Some clouds would help break it up so its not so white or a tad less on the exposure side would have helped a bit.  I''ll email you what I did to change the photo.  All I did was crop it a bit and change the saturation.', '2007-06-11 00:09:52.000000', '2007-06-11 00:11:42.000000', 0),
(3765236, 524881, 62634, '<td valign="top">Great capture. Go Fuji.</td>', 'Great capture. Go Fuji.', '2007-06-11 00:10:24.000000', NULL, 0),
