(3768550, 524272, 56672, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bosborne:</b></div><hr/><i> I have made this one of my favorites despite what the SC deems as a ''''failure''''. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nobody ever said it was a failure.  According to SC (since I haven''t seen an original, myself) it broke rules.  It could be the Mona Lisa and end up disqualified if it broke editing rules.  (He used a brush in basic editing.  Hah!)<br/> <br/>To quote one of my favorite movies:  "This isn''t Nam, Donnie, there are rules!"   It''s a great photo - I quite like it, but that doesn''t mean it deserves to retain its ribbon.  Do Olympic atheletes get to keep their golds if its discovered they juiced?  No.   Professional sports?  Oh, yeah, they get to keep their rings.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bosborne: I have made this one of my favorites despite what the SC deems as a ''''failure''''.   Nobody ever said it was a failure.  According to SC (since I haven''t seen an original, myself) it broke rules.  It could be the Mona Lisa and end up disqualified if it broke editing rules.  (He used a brush in basic editing.  Hah!) To quote one of my favorite movies:  "This isn''t Nam, Donnie, there are rules!"   It''s a great photo - I quite like it, but that doesn''t mean it deserves to retain its ribbon.  Do Olympic atheletes get to keep their golds if its discovered they juiced?  No.   Professional sports?  Oh, yeah, they get to keep their rings.', '2007-06-11 15:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3768948, 506980, 48954, '<td valign="top">oh my! gorgeous.</td>', 'oh my! gorgeous.', '2007-06-11 17:10:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(3769053, 524272, 61818, '<td valign="top">What a crock, I can''t believe you get DQ''d for using a standard darkroom technique.</td>', 'What a crock, I can''t believe you get DQ''d for using a standard darkroom technique.', '2007-06-11 17:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3769072, 525378, 70270, '<td valign="top">Wow, Jeff, I really like this image.  Great colors and composition.  I don''t see any excess noise here at all; what some call grain/noise I see as texture of the grasslands that enhances the feel of the image.  My only nit is that I might have eliminated the red dirt triangle on the left by shooting from a slightly different location and/or cropping, but that''s just an artistic choice that isn''t mine to make.</td>', 'Wow, Jeff, I really like this image.  Great colors and composition.  I don''t see any excess noise here at all; what some call grain/noise I see as texture of the grasslands that enhances the feel of the image.  My only nit is that I might have eliminated the red dirt triangle on the left by shooting from a slightly different location and/or cropping, but that''s just an artistic choice that isn''t mine to make.', '2007-06-11 17:48:24.000000', NULL, 0),
