(4699960, 524724, 48228, '<td valign="top"><b>WOW WOW WOW.....BREATHTAKING.....</b> <br/> <br/>This is truly a magical image..... To capture this at this very moment in time is amazing and I for one truly love it.....<br/> <br/>The detail of the center of the flower along with the praying mantis es just awesome.....<br/> <br/>Thank you for sharing this with us, and this  awesome image belongs in my favorites.....<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-05-13 19:38:49.</i></td>', 'WOW WOW WOW.....BREATHTAKING.....  This is truly a magical image..... To capture this at this very moment in time is amazing and I for one truly love it..... The detail of the center of the flower along with the praying mantis es just awesome..... Thank you for sharing this with us, and this  awesome image belongs in my favorites.....', '2008-05-13 20:37:58.000000', '2008-05-13 20:38:49.000000', 0),
(4753674, 511316, 56002, '<td valign="top">What a vast difference between the warm and cool tones here.  I am assuming that you used a polarizer on this one.  Sometimes I have troubles with my polarizer on the 10-22 (and I have an ultra thin model).  I have to be very careful with it (which is a drag).</td>', 'What a vast difference between the warm and cool tones here.  I am assuming that you used a polarizer on this one.  Sometimes I have troubles with my polarizer on the 10-22 (and I have an ultra thin model).  I have to be very careful with it (which is a drag).', '2008-06-06 09:30:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4774439, 524268, 30049, '<td valign="top">Picking a couple from the "favs" listed on your profile page.  Hope you don''t mind?<br/> <br/>One thing that is standing out is your approach to high contrast and extreme lighting situations; you''re not afraid to use this type of lighting to good effect in your compositions.  Very nice!<br/> <br/>I''ve also just noticed that you use Minolta glass with your Olympus.  That''s interesting.  I''d like to know what you use to convert this fine old glass over to your new DSLR.</td>', 'Picking a couple from the "favs" listed on your profile page.  Hope you don''t mind? One thing that is standing out is your approach to high contrast and extreme lighting situations; you''re not afraid to use this type of lighting to good effect in your compositions.  Very nice! I''ve also just noticed that you use Minolta glass with your Olympus.  That''s interesting.  I''d like to know what you use to convert this fine old glass over to your new DSLR.', '2008-06-18 10:51:23.000000', NULL, 0),
